Introduction
~~~~~~~~~~~~
This door protects from downloads below 9600 bps or whatever speed you
decide. This means for example that you can have 2400 bps users (or
V.32bis users calling an HST node) on your board but they will not be able
to download, only read and write mail etc.


Features
~~~~~~~~
The door won't disturb fast-modem users. It doesn't write anything if a
user passes speed check.

You may specify a time zone when the speed checks should be performed.
This means you can allow slow-modem users to download, but only at times
when the board activity usually is low.

If there is a time zone and a user is prevented from downloading, the
start and end times will be displayed, together with the current time.

You may specify an access level for overriding the speed checks. If you
trust your cosysops to be smart enough not to block the line with long
downloads, you could enter their access level in the config.

Also, you can configure a list of the users users who are always allowed
to download.


Installation
~~~~~~~~~~~~
Make the directory 'Doors:SpeedCheck', and copy 'SpeedCheck' and
'SpeedCheck.info' there.

The door is installed as the 'd' command of course.


/X 2.xx / SigmaExpress:

Add the following line to your BBS.CMD file:

-----Cut-here---------------------------------
*D        XM020Doors:SpeedCheck/SpeedCheck
-------Cut-here-------------------------------


/X 3.xx:

Copy the supplied icon "d.info" to "BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/" and edit its
tooltypes if they don't suit you.

Set the access for the door low enough so that all users with download
access will be able to run it. It doesn't really matter if you set too
low, because if a user passes the speed check, AmiExpress then checks that
he has access to download.


Configuration
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
The configuration icon Doors:SpeedCheck/SpeedCheck.info can contain the
following tooltypes:

LOWEST_SPEED=<baud rate>      - The lowest connect speed allowed for
                                downloading, for example 9600.

START=<time>                  - Start for the time zone when the speed
                                should be checked. Every user will be able
                                to download before and after this period.
                                The time must be in the format HH:MM.

END=<time>                    - End time for the period.

The bps will only be checked between START and END time. To never allow
downloads below the given speed, comment away the START or END tooltype.
START=END means download is always allowed.

ACS.OVERRIDE=<access level>   - If a user has this access level or higher
                                he will always be able to download, even
                                if his bps is too low. This tooltype is
                                optional.

NAME.x=<user name>            - The user written here will override the
                                speed check. First, NAME.1 is looked for,
                                then NAME.2, and so on, until it can't be
                                found.


